        "path": "_m/g/f/h/t/loch-ness-monster-wp/hero.jpg",
        "filename": "Loch Ness Monster Surgeon's photograph.jpg",
        "caption": "Original caption by Wide World Photos: This unretouched photograph, rushed here from London by radiograph, shows the famed Loch Ness monster as it was photographed by Dr. Robert Kenneth Wilson, noted surgeon of the London hospital when it appeared out of the waters of the Loch within 200 yards of where Dr. Wilson was seated with his camera. Scottish biologists' to whom Dr. Wilson's photographs were shown, decided the pictures were not those of any marine animal or fish known to inhabit British inland waters and none of the biologists would hazard a guess as to what the animal was. The pictures show a long neck and a small head poised above a bulky body.",
        "alt": "Original caption by Wide World Photos: This unretouched photograph, rushed here from London by radiograph, shows the famed Loch Ness monster as it was photographed by Dr. Robert Kenneth Wilson, noted surgeon of the London hospital when it appeared out of the waters of the Loch within 200 yards of where Dr. Wilson was seated with his camera. Scottish biologists' to whom Dr. Wilson's photographs were shown, decided the pictures were not those of any marine animal or fish known to inhabit British inland waters and none of the biologists would hazard a guess as to what the animal was. The pictures show a long neck and a small head poised above a bulky body.",
